   "en": "Mexico"
  },
  {
   "k": "1h0k7yc",
   "en": "Strategy"
  },
  {
   "k": "gpz78s",
   "en": "For this achievement, to annex ⟦0⟧, it is important to attack the ⟦1⟧ before they get too powerful as they have a guarantee over all countries in the western hemisphere if you don't have the ⟦2⟧ DLC enabled (and even with it enabled, the United States will get an event when you attack Mexico, and, on historical AI, will attempt to enforce peace, so, it amounts to the same thing.)",
   "frags": 3
  },
  {
   "k": "7tkm24",
   "en": "United States"
  },
  {
   "k": "1i7hp5l",
   "en": "Trial of Allegiance"
  },
  {
   "k": "1vot27b",
   "en": "To get ready for the invasion, save up political power then justify against ⟦0⟧. World tension will not get as high as if ⟦1⟧ is being justified against. Have a naval invasion to the ⟦2⟧ and a larger one from the Marshall Islands to Honolulu. Make a naval invasion from Honolulu to Los Angeles as well. The preparation time for that naval invasion will coincide with the naval invasions with the armies. Have the ships with the highest range in a different navy group (you start with two converted carriers with 4000 km range and a few heavy ships with 3000 km range, they are the only ones that can project naval supremacy all the way to California from Hawaii). This will allow range towards the west coast from Honolulu. Have part of the fleet protect the ocean towards the Philippines and a larger part of the fleet protect the invasion towards Honolulu. Have a few divisions with the naval invasion towards the ⟦3⟧ for reinforcement. To prepare the invasion of the ⟦4⟧, move the rest of the army to the Marshall islands as well. Declare war against the Philippines when ready.",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "1338jsc",
   "en": "Philippines"
  },
  {
   "k": "ug11gh",
   "en": "If you do this early (the party can kick off before the end of 1936), the Philippines and U.S. islands will be lightly defended or undefended. Your main difficulty will lie in having to deal with convoy raiding and supply line disruption (and the occasional reverse naval invasion). Your industry requires a lot of imported oil and steel, all of which needs to be imported via convoy, and you'll need even more convoys to first ship three armies worth of infantry to America, and then to supply them. You may want to assign dedicated task forces to convoy escort duty, and to start production of replacement convoys."
  },
  {
   "k": "10mci7g",
   "en": "Naval Invade the Philippines and Honolulu. Once Honolulu is captured, place divisions on the naval invasion to Los Angeles and send the rest of the army to Honolulu. send the level 2 ships to protect the naval invasion to Los Angeles. They are the only ships that can reach. The other ships may protect important areas as well. Naval invade Los Angeles when ready. There may be a naval skirmish against the Americans. Make sure the level 2 ships do not repair. This will force them to stay on the sea zone so that they can protect the army. While naval invading towards Los Angeles, Take Philippine land and make them capitulate. Once landed in Los Angeles, Send the bulk of the army there as well. Take land from the United States but do not capitulate them. They will not capitulate until Pennsylvania and Maryland gets captured. Capitulate ⟦0⟧ before the United States. Take all the territory from ⟦1⟧. Encircle and grind down the United States.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "1oww95l",
   "en": "After the war with the ⟦0⟧, there may be enough time to attack ⟦1⟧ before the Germans attack ⟦2⟧. If not, prepare war with the Allies. Once the Germans declare against the Allies, do that as well. Naval Invade from ⟦3⟧ to the British Isles.",
   "frags": 4
  },
